      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "The impact of myocardial revascularization without cardiopulmonary bypass (CPB) was evaluated in a series of consecutive patients with multivessel disease."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "From May 21, 1997 to November 30, 2000, 1,843 consecutive patients underwent isolated myocardial revascularization. From this total, 919 patients were done without CPB (group A, 49.9%) and 924 patients were done with CPB (group B, 50.1%). Patients that converted from without CPB to with CPB were included in group A. Thirty-three variables were evaluated with univariate and multivariate analysis to identify the independent variables predictive of higher incidence of early mortality, acute myocardial infarction, cerebrovascular accident, and early major events."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Early mortality was 2.2% (group A, 1.4%; group B, 3.0%; p = 0.016), acute myocardial infarction incidence was 1.8% (group A, 1.1%; group B, 2.6%; p = 0.027), cerebrovascular accident incidence was 0.9% (group A, 0.8%; group B, 1.0%; p = not significant), and early major events incidence was 6.7% (group A, 5.3%; group B, 8.2%; p < 0.001). Stepwise logistic regression analysis showed that CPB was an independent risk factor for higher mortality (odds ratio, 2.2; p = 0.0217), higher incidence of acute myocardial infarction (odds ratio, 2.5; p = 0.0185), and higher incidence of early major events (odds ratio, 1.8, p = 0.0034)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "When CPB was not used, patients experienced lower early mortality and incidences of acute myocardial infarction were less complicated, both at univariate analysis and stepwise logistic regression analysis."
        }
      ]},
